1
00:00:00,473 --> 00:00:02,328
I want to...

2
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:05,663
do couple-like things

3
00:00:08,008 --> 00:00:10,103
with you, too, Ryosuke.

4
00:00:18,086 --> 00:00:20,255
So?

5
00:00:20,255 --> 00:00:22,502
How far do couple things go?

6
00:00:22,502 --> 00:00:26,395
Huh? What do you mean, how far?

7
00:00:40,318 --> 00:00:43,393
Tell me. Hurry.

8
00:01:33,103 --> 00:01:35,176
Ryosuke?

9
00:02:26,021 --> 00:02:27,388
Huh?

10
00:02:33,886 --> 00:02:35,173
What the...

11
00:02:42,886 --> 00:02:44,458
Oh, good morning.

12
00:02:45,217 --> 00:02:46,684
Good morning.

13
00:02:48,884 --> 00:02:52,319
Oh, right. Are you okay?

14
00:02:52,319 --> 00:02:56,316
You drank quite a lot last night.
Are you feeling sick at all?

15
00:02:58,762 --> 00:03:00,264
Yeah...

16
00:03:02,248 --> 00:03:03,875
Wow, I'm sorry...

17
00:03:04,893 --> 00:03:06,593
I'm really sorry...

18
00:03:08,731 --> 00:03:11,472
Do you remember what happened yesterday?

19
00:03:11,472 --> 00:03:13,013
I...

20
00:03:14,393 --> 00:03:15,893
I remember.

21
00:03:29,557 --> 00:03:31,694
Did I scare you?

22
00:03:36,999 --> 00:03:38,652
No, you didn't.

23
00:03:44,871 --> 00:03:46,833
That's a relief.

24
00:04:06,731 --> 00:04:08,651
Are you hungry?

25
00:04:08,651 --> 00:04:11,121
Yeah, a little.

26
00:04:13,963 --> 00:04:16,371
Then let's eat.

27
00:04:16,371 --> 00:04:17,871
Sounds good.

28
00:04:28,094 --> 00:04:30,085
I used your shower.

29
00:04:34,581 --> 00:04:38,688
Wow, this looks really delicious.

30
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:41,392
Is tea okay?

31
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:43,575
Yeah.

32
00:04:47,836 --> 00:04:49,977
- It's good.
- Really?

33
00:04:49,977 --> 00:04:51,550
I'm glad.

34
00:04:52,578 --> 00:04:54,177
You cook, huh?

35
00:04:54,177 --> 00:04:56,857
Yeah, just a little.

36
00:05:05,965 --> 00:05:07,755
This is nice.

37
00:05:09,539 --> 00:05:12,217
Having you here when I wake up.

38
00:05:16,070 --> 00:05:17,370
Yeah.

39
00:05:18,202 --> 00:05:20,356
What do you mean, "Yeah"?

40
00:05:21,984 --> 00:05:25,437
It's just... I'm happy, too.

41
00:05:26,037 --> 00:05:27,604
You're happy?

42
00:05:28,328 --> 00:05:29,830
Yeah.

43
00:05:29,830 --> 00:05:31,233
What made you happy?

44
00:05:31,233 --> 00:05:33,324
- Specifically?
- Yeah.

45
00:05:34,283 --> 00:05:35,623
Everything.

46
00:05:35,623 --> 00:05:36,995
Everything?

47
00:05:38,881 --> 00:05:40,851
Tell me in detail.

48
00:05:43,494 --> 00:05:46,195
This moment. This time right now.

49
00:05:47,415 --> 00:05:48,981
I see.

50
00:05:56,985 --> 00:06:00,158
Wait, Taguchi?

51
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:03,042
Ryo...

52
00:06:04,905 --> 00:06:06,588
...suke.

53
00:06:07,626 --> 00:06:12,183
You're a little too close.

54
00:06:14,105 --> 00:06:16,479
Are you heading home?

55
00:06:16,479 --> 00:06:20,187
Yeah. I need to change
before going to work.

56
00:06:22,933 --> 00:06:24,713
I see.

57
00:06:29,640 --> 00:06:31,995
I don't wanna let you go.

58
00:06:44,491 --> 00:06:46,078
Just kidding.

59
00:07:12,407 --> 00:07:19,208
Did we manage to do
at least one couple thing?

60
00:07:25,916 --> 00:07:27,338
I'm sorry...

61
00:07:28,758 --> 00:07:32,764
Sorry, wait a second.

62
00:07:36,879 --> 00:07:39,252
If we go further, I won't stop.

63
00:08:03,358 --> 00:08:06,211
Shiori, you're the best girlfriend ever.

64
00:08:09,077 --> 00:08:12,193
And you, Ryosuke,

65
00:08:12,193 --> 00:08:16,291
are the best boyfriend.

66
00:08:32,410 --> 00:08:33,722
Are you good on time?

67
00:08:33,722 --> 00:08:35,963
Yeah, I should be fine.

68
00:08:35,963 --> 00:08:37,976
See you at work.

69
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:39,072
Okay.

70
00:09:43,522 --> 00:09:46,091
We'll go ahead with this then.

71
00:09:46,091 --> 00:09:49,006
Thank you. I'll take care of it.

72
00:09:49,625 --> 00:09:52,609
Mr. Kashiwagi! I compiled the test data.

73
00:09:52,609 --> 00:09:55,174
Wow, that was fast. I'm impressed.

74
00:09:55,174 --> 00:09:59,105
Because you said you wanted it
as soon as possible, Mr. Kashiwagi.

75
00:09:59,105 --> 00:10:03,346
Sorry about that.
Seriously, this helps a lot. Thank you.

76
00:10:05,365 --> 00:10:09,215
His communication skills are amazing.

77
00:10:12,390 --> 00:10:13,940
They really are.

78
00:10:13,940 --> 00:10:16,933
It's hard to believe
he's only been here a week.

79
00:10:21,062 --> 00:10:22,791
Come in.

80
00:10:22,791 --> 00:10:24,124
Excuse me. I'm coming in.

81
00:10:24,124 --> 00:10:26,204
Good work.

82
00:10:28,363 --> 00:10:29,336
Hello there.

83
00:10:29,336 --> 00:10:30,540
Good work.

84
00:10:30,540 --> 00:10:32,349
- Hello.
- Hi.

85
00:10:33,899 --> 00:10:35,633
Sorry for taking up your time.

86
00:10:35,633 --> 00:10:36,860
- Not at all.
- It's fine.

87
00:10:36,860 --> 00:10:39,993
I want to talk about
the school for the field test.

88
00:10:39,993 --> 00:10:43,622
This is your Alma mater, right?

89
00:10:43,622 --> 00:10:47,204
Could you two go together
to say hello before the test begins?

90
00:10:49,041 --> 00:10:50,138
Understood.

91
00:10:50,138 --> 00:10:51,283
- Sure.
- Glad to hear that.

92
00:10:51,283 --> 00:10:53,921
The head of one of the grades
is our point person.

93
00:10:53,921 --> 00:10:55,738
You have their contact info, right?

94
00:10:55,738 --> 00:10:56,848
Yes.

95
00:10:56,848 --> 00:11:00,117
[Kanagawa Prefectural
Tsurushiro High School]

96
00:11:10,815 --> 00:11:13,235
Sorry! Did you wait long?

97
00:11:13,235 --> 00:11:15,308
No, not at all.

98
00:11:15,308 --> 00:11:17,161
- Let's go.
- Okay.

99
00:11:22,646 --> 00:11:24,160
You're going to Tsurushiro?

100
00:11:24,160 --> 00:11:28,430
Yeah, I'm heading to a meeting
with Kashiwagi.

101
00:11:29,391 --> 00:11:32,505
I think you'll join us
when the field test starts,

102
00:11:32,505 --> 00:11:34,998
so let's do our best, okay?

103
00:11:37,155 --> 00:11:38,313
Sure.

104
00:11:40,985 --> 00:11:43,394
<i>Remember your last client?</i>

105
00:11:43,394 --> 00:11:45,339
Yes, I remember.

106
00:11:45,339 --> 00:11:48,959
<i>We're trying to start another project there.</i>

107
00:11:48,959 --> 00:11:51,357
<i>We want you to come, Taguchi.</i>

108
00:11:54,617 --> 00:11:56,394
You see...

109
00:11:56,394 --> 00:11:57,634
Yeah?

110
00:11:59,905 --> 00:12:04,223
I mean, who's our point person at the school?

111
00:12:04,223 --> 00:12:07,396
It's Mr. Nomoto. He's the head teacher
for one of the grades now.

112
00:12:07,396 --> 00:12:08,956
Oh, the guidance counselor?

113
00:12:08,956 --> 00:12:10,163
Yep.

114
00:12:11,563 --> 00:12:13,302
How old is he now?

115
00:12:13,302 --> 00:12:15,360
Well, not sure.

116
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,409
Maybe in his fifties?

117
00:12:17,409 --> 00:12:19,396
Probably around that age.

118
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,037
It's been a while.

119
00:12:28,626 --> 00:12:30,616
I'm doing well.

120
00:12:33,476 --> 00:12:35,698
How do you still remember that?

121
00:12:35,698 --> 00:12:38,549
Please forget it...

122
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:43,774
Yes.

123
00:12:43,774 --> 00:12:47,281
She's here. Do you want to speak to her?

124
00:12:48,977 --> 00:12:50,495
It's Mr. Nomoto.

125
00:12:53,755 --> 00:12:55,493
Hello?

126
00:12:56,751 --> 00:13:00,049
Yes, this is Yamane. It's been a long time.

127
00:13:02,407 --> 00:13:07,543
Yes, that's right.
It really is a coincidence. Yes.

128
00:13:08,615 --> 00:13:11,277
I'm really looking forward to it too.

129
00:13:13,075 --> 00:13:17,961
Yes, I look forward to seeing you.
Thank you.

130
00:13:22,201 --> 00:13:25,755
[Can we head home together today?]

131
00:13:36,663 --> 00:13:38,003
Hey there.

132
00:13:38,683 --> 00:13:40,050
Hi.

133
00:13:50,003 --> 00:13:52,463
Were you okay that night?

134
00:13:52,463 --> 00:13:55,187
I had a terrible hangover after that.

135
00:13:56,194 --> 00:13:57,684
Oh, really?

136
00:14:06,103 --> 00:14:07,639
[I'm not sure yet.]

137
00:14:07,639 --> 00:14:11,443
[If I don't have to work overtime,
I wanna go home with you!]

138
00:14:20,061 --> 00:14:21,609
Is it Ms. Yamane?

139
00:14:24,204 --> 00:14:25,424
Yeah.

140
00:14:27,145 --> 00:14:29,009
Do you go home together?

141
00:14:30,450 --> 00:14:33,028
Only when our timing lines up.

142
00:14:33,028 --> 00:14:35,150
I see.

143
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:39,256
Wow, I never thought
I'd see you make that face.

144
00:14:40,408 --> 00:14:43,103
I couldn't have imagined this in high school.

145
00:14:52,935 --> 00:14:55,273
After you transferred schools,

146
00:14:56,150 --> 00:14:59,662
Ms. Yamane was really depressed.

147
00:15:03,820 --> 00:15:08,245
Well, I was just worried about her from afar.

148
00:15:14,347 --> 00:15:15,694
Bye then.

149
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:23,773
Hello. This is Kashiwagi from Meigakusha.

150
00:15:23,773 --> 00:15:26,667
Yes, thank you for calling back.

151
00:15:30,207 --> 00:15:32,495
That's why this sucks.

152
00:15:36,453 --> 00:15:43,369
We'll share the schedule we have now
with the development team and...

153
00:15:43,369 --> 00:15:46,372
Ms. Yamane, you can stop here for today.

154
00:15:46,372 --> 00:15:48,139
Wait, but...

155
00:15:48,139 --> 00:15:50,503
Don't you have plans with Taguchi?

156
00:15:50,503 --> 00:15:51,429
Huh?

157
00:15:51,429 --> 00:15:54,619
I'll head home
right after I finish this part.

158
00:15:56,130 --> 00:15:57,517
Good work.

159
00:16:00,313 --> 00:16:02,228
Good work.

160
00:16:27,963 --> 00:16:29,130
You're here.

161
00:16:29,130 --> 00:16:31,088
Hey there.

162
00:16:31,088 --> 00:16:32,715
Let's go.

163
00:16:32,715 --> 00:16:34,022
Okay.

164
00:16:42,782 --> 00:16:45,172
What should we do for dinner?

165
00:16:45,172 --> 00:16:46,552
Oh...

166
00:16:51,677 --> 00:16:54,850
It's pretty late.

167
00:16:54,850 --> 00:16:57,310
Wanna stop by a restaurant?

168
00:17:11,748 --> 00:17:14,979
You seem happy today, Yamane.

169
00:17:14,979 --> 00:17:16,906
Did something good happen?

170
00:17:18,005 --> 00:17:22,784
Well, there's something
I'm kind of looking forward to after this.

171
00:17:22,784 --> 00:17:27,467
Well, there's hardly any work left,
so you can go home for today.

172
00:17:28,682 --> 00:17:33,554
Thank you! Then I'll head out first.

173
00:17:33,554 --> 00:17:35,541
See you.

174
00:17:36,837 --> 00:17:38,661
Huh?

175
00:17:38,661 --> 00:17:40,503
Is something wrong?

176
00:17:40,503 --> 00:17:44,331
The book title and barcode info don't match.

177
00:17:44,331 --> 00:17:47,013
Maybe they were stuck on the wrong data.

178
00:17:47,013 --> 00:17:51,700
Probably. A bunch of books came in at once
the other day.

179
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:55,308
We'll need to redo them all.

180
00:17:55,308 --> 00:17:57,227
I'll do it.

181
00:17:57,227 --> 00:17:58,440
You will?

182
00:17:58,440 --> 00:18:01,339
I don't have practice today, so I'm free.

183
00:18:03,792 --> 00:18:06,402
Yamane, see you.

184
00:18:15,551 --> 00:18:17,058
Wait...

185
00:18:21,316 --> 00:18:23,524
Kashiwagi!

186
00:18:23,524 --> 00:18:25,651
You're still here!

187
00:18:26,499 --> 00:18:28,921
Didn't you have plans with Taguchi?

188
00:18:28,921 --> 00:18:31,116
I told him to go on ahead today.

189
00:18:31,116 --> 00:18:35,473
This report is due today, right?
I'll help you finish it.

190
00:18:49,354 --> 00:18:50,461
Yamane!

191
00:18:50,461 --> 00:18:52,907
<i>At first, I thought you were a quiet girl.</i>

192
00:18:52,907 --> 00:18:55,504
Here's this month's library newsletter.

193
00:18:55,504 --> 00:18:59,019
Ms. Kawatani wants it on the bulletin board.

194
00:18:59,019 --> 00:19:01,050
Thank you.

195
00:19:03,048 --> 00:19:04,495
<i>That's why...</i>

196
00:19:05,541 --> 00:19:07,734
Yamane! Good morning.

197
00:19:07,734 --> 00:19:09,882
Good morning.

198
00:19:09,882 --> 00:19:12,212
<i>It's like I was overstepping.</i>

199
00:19:12,212 --> 00:19:13,734
Yamane!

200
00:19:14,619 --> 00:19:16,004
Good work!

201
00:19:16,004 --> 00:19:18,057
- Good work.
<i>- Every time I saw Yamane,</i>

202
00:19:18,057 --> 00:19:19,785
- PE lesson?
- <i>I'd call out to her.</i>

203
00:19:19,785 --> 00:19:20,966
Yeah.

204
00:19:21,968 --> 00:19:24,263
<i>- But...</i>
- Wait!

205
00:19:26,404 --> 00:19:28,792
I'll help too.

206
00:19:28,792 --> 00:19:31,898
It'll get done faster with more people.

207
00:19:31,898 --> 00:19:34,846
Really? Sorry, thank you.

208
00:19:34,846 --> 00:19:37,938
<i>Yamane doesn't need me looking out for her.</i>

209
00:19:37,938 --> 00:19:41,166
I'll check the shelves over there.

210
00:19:41,166 --> 00:19:43,945
<i>She can think and act for herself.</i>

211
00:19:43,945 --> 00:19:47,026
I'll start from the other side.

212
00:19:47,026 --> 00:19:48,739
Thank you.

213
00:19:50,463 --> 00:19:55,015
<i>I realized how presumptuous I was,
thinking I had to check in on her.</i>

214
00:19:56,490 --> 00:19:58,515
<i>It felt arrogant.</i>

215
00:20:15,678 --> 00:20:18,919
I'm heading over there. See you at school.

216
00:20:18,919 --> 00:20:20,292
Okay.

217
00:20:20,292 --> 00:20:21,752
Bye.

218
00:20:24,469 --> 00:20:28,515
<i>Honestly, they were an unexpected pair.</i>

219
00:20:29,181 --> 00:20:32,188
I'll take it. How much?

220
00:20:32,188 --> 00:20:34,318
No, it's fine.

221
00:20:34,318 --> 00:20:35,320
Here.

222
00:20:39,239 --> 00:20:40,812
Thank you.

223
00:20:47,193 --> 00:20:50,958
So, is that all?

224
00:20:50,958 --> 00:20:52,418
Yeah.

225
00:20:52,418 --> 00:20:54,352
Bye, then.

226
00:20:56,213 --> 00:21:00,223
Taguchi! Thanks for this.

227
00:21:00,223 --> 00:21:01,476
Sure.

228
00:21:11,106 --> 00:21:14,383
Are we having an after-party
after the culture fest?

229
00:21:14,383 --> 00:21:16,571
Of course we are.

230
00:21:16,571 --> 00:21:17,757
Huh? Aren't we?

231
00:21:17,757 --> 00:21:21,075
I was wondering how long we'd stay.

232
00:21:21,075 --> 00:21:22,771
Everyone's going.

233
00:21:22,771 --> 00:21:26,935
But honestly,
won't it feel awkward inviting Taguchi?

234
00:21:28,038 --> 00:21:30,055
Yeah, that's true.

235
00:21:30,887 --> 00:21:33,633
He's good-looking, though.

236
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:37,691
He seems like a nice guy.

237
00:21:37,691 --> 00:21:38,918
Huh?

238
00:21:38,918 --> 00:21:42,288
I heard he's close with Yamane.

239
00:21:43,319 --> 00:21:45,045
Yamane?

240
00:21:45,045 --> 00:21:48,930
From Class 4.
They're both library committee members.

241
00:21:51,172 --> 00:21:53,314
Wait, he's Yamane's type?

242
00:21:53,314 --> 00:21:54,626
What do you mean?

243
00:21:54,626 --> 00:21:55,922
Well...

244
00:21:57,371 --> 00:21:59,890
Pass me the red pen. Red pen.

245
00:21:59,890 --> 00:22:02,417
- Red?
- Here.

246
00:22:02,417 --> 00:22:04,283
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

247
00:22:05,659 --> 00:22:09,806
<i>From that casual single line...</i>

248
00:22:10,622 --> 00:22:12,222
Taguchi?

249
00:22:13,601 --> 00:22:18,774
<i>I never imagined
it would turn out like this...</i>

250
00:22:20,465 --> 00:22:22,558
<i>I never saw it coming.</i>

251
00:22:24,118 --> 00:22:26,646
So did Taguchi drop out in the end?

252
00:22:26,646 --> 00:22:29,534
No, he didn't drop out. He transferred.

253
00:22:29,534 --> 00:22:31,238
Really?

254
00:22:31,238 --> 00:22:33,198
Why?

255
00:22:33,198 --> 00:22:34,918
No clue.

256
00:22:49,953 --> 00:22:51,607
<i>Gosh...</i>

257
00:22:52,995 --> 00:22:54,578
<i>I...</i>

258
00:22:54,578 --> 00:22:56,657
See you at school.

259
00:22:56,657 --> 00:22:58,103
Okay.

260
00:22:58,103 --> 00:23:01,882
- Bye.
<i>- I was in love.</i>

261
00:23:01,882 --> 00:23:03,769
<i>With Yamane.</i>

262
00:23:13,232 --> 00:23:14,799
Hey...

263
00:23:21,921 --> 00:23:24,142
I can say this now, but...

264
00:23:27,147 --> 00:23:28,554
I...

265
00:23:30,447 --> 00:23:33,370
Mr. Taguchi is leaving the project.

266
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:34,553
What?

267
00:23:34,553 --> 00:23:37,206
Shiori, don't worry about it.

268
00:23:37,206 --> 00:23:38,960
Did something happen with him?

269
00:23:38,960 --> 00:23:43,456
It's easier to speak your true feelings
if you feel loved.

270
00:23:43,456 --> 00:23:45,144
Did you date before?

271
00:23:45,144 --> 00:23:46,590
No.

272
00:23:46,590 --> 00:23:49,036
Don't talk to me anymore.

273
00:23:49,036 --> 00:23:51,118
Putting distance between you again...

274
00:23:51,118 --> 00:23:53,557
Are you gonna regret it for years again?

275
00:23:53,557 --> 00:23:59,929
I wonder if Ryosuke is being honest
with his own feelings.
